          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Dainik Bhaskar and Indian Publishers File CCI Complaint Against Google Over AI Search Revenue Sharing",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "Dainik Bhaskar, one of India's largest Hindi-language media groups, has joined other publishers in filing a complaint with the Competition Commission of India against Google, citing concerns over unfair revenue sharing as AI-driven search reduces traffic to news websites. The publishers allege that Google's AI-powered search summaries are displaying their content without adequate compensation. This filing marks a significant escalation in the global publisher-versus-platform dispute, now formally entering India's competition regulatory arena.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/05/223-dainik-bhaskar-publishers-file-cci-case-google-revenue-sharing/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
